cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this standard or validator, please cite it as below."
title: "tcat-data-standard: schema and validator for transient-kinetics and operando-spectroscopy datasets"
abstract: >-
  Machine-readable definition of a valid transient-kinetics dataset, with a
  validator that runs in CI as an ingestion gate. Profiles the TRACE-AI reporting
  guidelines and extends them for transient kinetics: parameterised perturbation
  protocols that are exactly regenerable, a shared time base across
  simultaneously-acquired modalities, sensor models as versioned citable
  artifacts, and parameter uncertainty stored as a sample rather than a summary.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-20"
license: MIT
